6,1,"How do we propagate errors?"],["462327fc_69291c28",44,-6,1,"should we also send API Key separately or it will be included in this URL? Sending and displaying URL + API Key might be less error-prone for a user and they won't need to figure out in which format…"],["5443f6fb_18d9fb5f",45,-6,1,"nit: same, check headers"],["5e61a606_68c66347",43,-6,1,"nit: missing header"],["9a3dbd9d_3c9c6aa7",43,-6,1,"nit: missing header"],["10c99a81_20b18cac",44,-5,1,"Actually, we might just pass URL + API key as variables and therefore simplify Mojo interface: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:docs/webui/webui_in_chrome.md;l=275-277?q=webui%…"],["2d73a1f5_494d1abc",41,-3,0,"Optional: If possible we can make it public. https://www.chromium.org/issue-tracking/googler-guidelines/"],["7449de11_0bcfa74b",44,-3,1,"This looks like a generic meta-IPC: ``` union Response { string response; string error; }; interface Handler { SendRequest(string request) => (Response response); }; ``` While I understand the desire…"],["91818191_a217acfc",46,-3,0,"Can you add a .catch() block here so we can determine the error during debugging?"],["9dcab4dc_254c1341",47,-3,1,"The `..` directory already contains file://components/legion/OWNERS What about removing it here? I am asking, because this is useless, and I am also not sure about the priority in between L1-2 and L4."],["01eacae6_da60f0ff",45,0,1,"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/security/mojo.md#do-not-define-unimplemented-methods"],["07a4775e_be5eda25",44,0,0,"can you please feature-bind this interface? (`RuntimeFeature=YourFeatureName`)"],["0d73e487_1f566b09",44,0,0,"Can we add `(string? error)` here?"],["ee8bfb69_da966002",48,0,0,"can we `std::make_unique<Client>(...)`?"]],0,1276],[7138341,20403,4,0.248,0.173,[[50,7]],[],0,1277],[7150878,20409,132,3.856,3.092,[[50,0.479,8,64],[13,0.275,61,37],[17,0.211,300,27],[51,0.035,3,4]],[],0,1278],[7166712,20411,100,1.654,1.364,[[30,0.992,7,2088],[43,0.006,4,12],[54,0.001,0,2]],[],0,1279],[7170546,20412,8,0.406,0.291,[[50,0.5,9,4],[52,0.5,1,4]],[["105485f4_f00e419c",48,-1,1,"I dont think we should hardcode the model name here."]],0,1280],[7167088,20412,82,1.654,1.364,[[30,8]],[["0c9e0334_e152f62b",49,-2,1,"do you still need this if already defined in the interface?"],["4b138d79_a000b205",50,-2,1,"I'd ideally move it to a separate file, but not a code owner, so delegating review to Sophie."]],0,1281],[7172043,20418,296,7.601,6.192,[[28,0.487,8,145],[30,0.471,9,140],[4,0.026,22,7],[50,0.016,10,4]],[["0e870bd5_94a38f6e",51,-7,0,"It seems like the logic how to create a fetcher is splitted (this file + optimization_guide_keyed_service.cc), could we move it into 1 place so it's easier to follow?"],["2ab6d636_2585e47e",52,-7,1,"Shouldn't this be behind buildflag?"],["627d0cd2_c1487d66",52,-7,1,"put behind buildflag?"],["aade5590_4493917d",52,-7,0,"This will execute on iOS IIUC, not Android."],["5ea27a37_f42609c8",52,-6,1,"would prefer for this to not be in service creation here. can we maybe make it an option in the api to specify the mechanism? and for now - just do a hard CHECK if the feature doesn't match zss?"],["71606e79_efff7710",53,-6,1,"need to update ios keyed service to send this in (but anyway - see other comments)"],["75ab602c_f13343fe",54,-6,1,"im not entirely sure this flag belongs in opt guide but in contextual_cueing where the zss feature itself is. i think it would make sense to control it as an option as part of the mes api"],["e5134287_65ea1c2a",52,-6,1,"CreateFetcher (capital c)"],["042202bc_864b5a82",55,-5,1,"nit: please add missing headers so they are already included in model_execution_fetcher.h Same applies to other files. https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Include_What_You_Use"],["221bfca0_807daa34",56,-5,1,"nit: can you make this ModelExecutionServiceType (when i was reading through the code - i was confused why this wasnt a pointer and then only realized it was an enum)"],["3a1a94ed_66cae4e0",51,-5,1,"non-blocking nit: I'd try to avoid using CHECKs as it increases the risk of a crash, especially given that there are a lot of permutations of MES features/execution services/feature flags. just a…"],["708949dc_b22ca044",56,-5,1,"period after this"],["a95d7ab2_17bfadba",51,-5,0,"same"],["abf0e549_00e48d6c",57,-5,0,"nit: isn't it default behavior when you use strict mock?"],["e5d30ee6_ced951ca",58,-5,1,"why do you need this? theres already the fwd declare"],["3f8047ba_d13b8e2a",56,-2,1,"can we add a comment here that this should only be used for zss and to please consult the team if they want to learn more."],["de22c58c_85ccb661",51,-1,1,"nit: Can you please update this comment to mention that this part has to be updated if we want to support other features, so that it is easier to point/find the code which needs to be changed?"]],0,1282],[7185084,20419,97,2.087,1.667,[[4,0.233,23,21],[17,0.217,301,24],[30,0.2,10,20],[28,0.167,9,15],[55,0.108,1,11],[56,0.025,0,2],[57,0.025,0,2],[58,0.025,0,2]],[],0,1283],[7208955,20423,5,0.259,0.185,[[59,0]],[],0,1284],[7213421,20423,472,0.051,0.038,[[60,0.714,1,340],[61,0.166,7,79],[15,0.056,128,25],[17,0.044,302,19],[62,0.021,7,9]],[],0,1285],[7209479,20430,276,7.601,6.192,[[28,0.94,10,262],[56,0.06,1,14]],[["09be75f8_c315f39c",59,-10,0,"These might not be enough. Since outputs can be non deterministic. There can be strings like: \"Here are 5 suggestions:\". Since this is a prototype, we can consider adding a post-processing step to…"],["3818c10d_1a495664",59,-10,0,"Can you please sanitize these strings (remove newlines/control characters) before appending to the request? Same for below."],["61c8e99b_9fbbfea4",59,-10,0,"nit: Until we don't know how to store them can we add a DLOG in case we need to debug it?"],["eb708010_1c23802c",41,-10,1,"nit: prototype"],["059a7c23_92a97e8e",59,-5,0,"instead of sending the ZSS request/response proto back and forth - I think it'd be easier to just have this be wrapped in a ExecuteRequest/Response proto so we can get some of the monitoring slicing…"],["c1f3be17_124b94be",60,-5,1,"nit: can remove options="],["f53c30f9_1b3555b1",61,-5,1,"zerostatesuggestions"],["10038827_4fb54ca8",59,-3,0,"Hi Christian, do we need '()' here? if you want to segregate content from prompt maybe using control tokens will be better. Also wouldn't it be better to have this prompt after the content?"],["2303191b_fb83a29f",59,-3,1,"I am more concerned here about parsing and handling UTF-8 encoding correctly, as this function does not seem to support non-ASCII encoding. Can we have unit tests that it works correctly for…"],["6c05decf_d2b8ef3c",59,-3,0,"non-blocking: Would be nice to make sure that we do not mess-up with UTF-8 encoding here."],["76e8fedd_31f50ea3",59,-3,0,"Can we have a unit test for this function??"],["312e0d6a_7def5434",59,0,0,"just curious - are you planning on moving the metrics out of the other impl (particularly the latency one) in a future CL to be shared so we have something ok to compare with in the dark launch?"],["5d9532ac_4f270d09",62,0,0,"❤️"],["98903cda_c78cd223",62,0,1,"nit: could you please use base::test::TestFuture instead? It will be easier to read the code"],["ef58e51b_c3d78a26",59,0,1,"i probably care more about a test for this part rather than the ZSS specific implementation now that the CL you mentioned has landed"]],0,1285],[7261300,20437,13,0.421,0.3,[[51,0.688,4,10],[50,0.188,11,2],[19,0.125,89,1]],[],0,1286],[7320240,20446,18,0.804,0.589,[[12,0.52,45,12],[63,0.48,1,6]],[],0,1287]]}